change:
  id: CHG-014
  title: Make the scorer capable of enforcing a declared mutation contract
  status: delivered
  intent: Give PhenotypeFitnessScorer an entry point that receives a MutationContract and a typed channel of observed results keyed by its declared required_evidence ids, so a declared gate can be enforced. This builds the capability; it does not migrate the wired promotion path, so RISK-002 stays open.
  audience_level: developer
  relates_to:
    - RISK-002
    - ARCH-001
    - CON-002
    - SYS-001

deltas:
  - op: MODIFIED
    capability: mutation-fitness-loop
    requirement: On its contract-aware entry point only, the scorer decides against a contract's declared required-evidence ids in addition to its structural fixed gates, and weights against the objective set that contract declares. The contractless entry point is unchanged.
    scenarios:
      - id: S1
        when: a contract declares a required_evidence id and no observed result is supplied for it
        then: the candidate is discarded on a hard gate naming that declared id
        and:
          - a passing result for any other id, declared or undeclared, does not satisfy the missing one
      - id: S2
        when: a contract declares a required_evidence id and an observed result for it reports failure
        then: the candidate is discarded on a hard gate naming that id
        and:
          - the outcome is recorded against that id in the audit map
      - id: S3
        when: two observed results are supplied for the same declared id and either reports failure
        then: the candidate is discarded on a hard gate naming that id
        and:
          - a passing result never masks a failing result for the same declared id
      - id: S4
        when: every declared required_evidence id has a passing observed result
        then: the declared-evidence gate contributes no discard and scoring proceeds to the weighted objectives
      - id: S5
        when: an observed result is supplied for an id the contract did not declare
        then: it is recorded as an inert non-gate entry in the existing FitnessResult objectives map and cannot satisfy or weaken any declared gate
        and:
          - no audit key is ever written twice: declared and undeclared ids are disjoint by construction, and an id colliding with a structural gate key is rejected outright rather than merged
      - id: S6
        when: a candidate passes every declared required_evidence id but fails a structural fixed gate such as non-empty realization
        then: the candidate is still discarded on that structural gate
        and:
          - declared-evidence gates are additional to the structural gates, never a replacement for them
      - id: S7
        when: a declared-evidence gate decides an outcome
        then: it is emitted through FitnessSignalId as a canonical subject invariant, and a failure voids the candidate as DISCARD rather than reducing a weighted score
        and:
          - CON-002 severity classes are not enforced anywhere yet, so integrity is expressed as voiding, not as a severity field
      - id: S8
        when: a caller scores without supplying a contract
        then: the existing fixed-gate behaviour and DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES weighting are preserved unchanged for that call
      - id: S10
        when: a declared or observed evidence id canonicalises to a key a structural gate already owns, such as deterministic_checks
        then: scoring rejects the input rather than merging, because a merge could report a passing structural gate for a candidate whose checks failed
      - id: S9
        when: the wired promotion path evaluates a candidate after this change
        then: it still uses the contractless entry point, so a declared required_evidence id is still not enforced end to end
        and:
          - RISK-002 remains open until a later change migrates the wired path
          - this pins the bridge's delegate call; it does not catch a rewire that swaps the scorer at EvolveRunner, which needs the migration's own component coverage

acceptance:
  - scenario: S1
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceIdHasNoObservedResult
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S2
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.discardsWhenADeclaredEvidenceIdReportsFailure
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S3
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.aPassingResultCannotMaskAFailingResultForTheSameId
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S4
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.proceedsToObjectivesWhenEveryDeclaredEvidenceIdPasses
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S5
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.undeclaredEvidenceCannotSatisfyADeclaredGate
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S6
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.structuralGatesStillApplyWhenDeclaredEvidencePasses
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S7
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.declaredEvidenceGatesAreEmittedUnderTheCanonicalScheme
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S8
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.contractlessScoringPreservesTheExistingGates
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S10
    test_id: deterministic/ContractAwareFitnessTest.evidenceCannotOverwriteAStructuralGateOutcome
    layer: unit
  - scenario: S9
    test_id: deterministic/PhenotypeBridgeScorerTest.theWiredBridgeStillUsesTheContractlessEntryPoint
    layer: unit

tasks:
  - id: T1
    slice: add a typed RequiredEvidenceResult carrying its own evidence id, a pass/fail outcome and a diagnostic, supplied to the scorer as a collection rather than a map so two results for one id remain distinguishable
    status: completed
  - id: T2
    slice: add the S8 and S9 characterisation tests first, green on write, so a regression to the contractless path or a change of wired delegate fails during T3 to T5 rather than after them
    status: completed
  - id: T2b
    slice: add failing unit coverage for S1 through S7 against the new contract-aware entry point
    status: completed
  - id: T3
    slice: add the contract-aware scorer entry point, enforcing declared required_evidence in addition to the structural gates
    status: completed
  - id: T4
    slice: emit declared-evidence gate outcomes under the CON-002 canonical subject-invariant scheme and classify them as integrity outcomes
    status: completed
  - id: T5
    slice: read the contract's declared objective set for both the objective-presence gate and the weighting on the contract-aware path only, leaving the contractless path on DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES; reading one from the contract and the other from the global would become incoherent the moment the validator is relaxed
    status: completed
  - id: T6
    slice: record undeclared results as inert non-gate entries written before gate outcomes, per S5
    status: completed
  - id: T8
    slice: surface a failed declared-evidence gate's diagnostic in the decision record. FitnessResult carries only Map<String, Double>, so the reason a candidate was discarded cannot reach a reporter today; the diagnostic is required at the input boundary but has no output carrier
    status: pending
  - id: T7
    slice: record what remains in RISK-002, CHG-002 T4b, README and wiki, and open the missing loop-side task: producing and accepting a MutationContract inside MutationEvaluationLoop is currently only a HANDOFF backlog line and a CHG-005 risk note, not a tracked task in any change. RISK-002 stays open
    status: completed

non_goals:
  - migrating MutationEvaluationLoop from Mutation onto MutationContract, which is the reason RISK-002 stays open. T7 must open a task for it, because today it exists only as a HANDOFF backlog line and a CHG-005 risk note
  - changing FitnessScorer or PhenotypeBridgeScorer, whose two-argument call is the wired path
  - retiring PhenotypeFitnessScorerTest.everyOperatorSharesTheObjectiveSetTheScorerAssumes, which stays load-bearing while the wired path weights against DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES
  - relaxing MutationContractValidator.requireDeterministicObjectives so an accepted contract may declare a non-default objective set
  - making behavioral_safety variable, wiring the benchmarks module, or ranking several candidates per generation
  - letting any model-produced judgement reach a score, a gate or a promotion decision

risks:
  - this change builds a capability the wired path does not use, so nothing about live promotion improves until the Mutation-to-MutationContract migration lands. S9 exists so that gap is asserted rather than quietly assumed, and T7 forbids closing RISK-002
  - the contractless entry point is the wired one, so the weaker path is the default rather than a fallback. A new caller could adopt it; a follow-up should add an architecture guard once the migration target exists
  - the contract-aware path can only weight against a declared objective set that MutationContractValidator currently rejects, because requireDeterministicObjectives forces every accepted contract onto the operator defaults and every operator shares DEFAULT_OBJECTIVES. Until that validator rule is revisited, T5's behaviour is reachable only in scorer-level tests
  - enforcing declared evidence will discard candidates that previously promoted once the wired path migrates, which is the intended correction but changes recorded outcomes for any repeat of an earlier experiment
  - a failed declared-evidence gate records only 0.0. Its diagnostic is required from the caller but has no carrier in FitnessResult, so the reason for a discard is not yet surfaced anywhere. Tracked as T8
  - FitnessResult copies its objectives with Map.copyOf, which does not preserve insertion order, so no caller can rely on audit iteration order. Correctness therefore does not depend on write order: keys are disjoint by construction and colliding ids are rejected
